          "content": "**Q. On which item does Imran’s family spend the most and the second most?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.342,
            0.791,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Imran’s family spends the most on food and the second most on house rent."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.373,
            0.684,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "**Q.2. Is the cost of electricity about one-half the cost of education?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.406,
            0.22,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.437,
            0.683,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Is the cost of education less than one-fourth the cost of food?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.469,
            0.777,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes. Cost of education = Rs. 800 and cost of food = Rs $3 4 0 0 = 4 \\mathrm { ~ x ~ }$ Rs 850"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.501,
            0.603,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": "So, cost of education = less than one-fourth of cost of food."
        },
